{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "We have only one completed experiment (config_001: RNA-only, singleprofile, PCA → 48.5% acc), so evidence is extremely sparse. The most fundamental uncertainty in a multimodal cellular profiling study is whether the image modality carries useful signal at all. config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is the cleanest test of this: it matches config_001 in profile setting (singleprofile) and overall simplicity (no aggregation, no fusion), changing only the modality from RNA to image. If image-only accuracy is close to or exceeds 48.5%, it confirms that image features are a viable signal source and justifies investing budget in multimodal fusion experiments. If it is substantially lower, we learn that RNA is the dominant modality and can focus subsequent experiments on RNA encoder/aggregation choices rather than fusion strategies. This single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the highest-level design axis (modality) before committing budget to more granular questions like encoder choice, aggregation, or fusion type."
}

